    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0747" n="727" xml:id="pg727"/>

                <head>313. Letter From the Deputy Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs
                        Johnson) to the Deputy
                    Secretary of Defense (Gilpatric)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d313-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                        1962</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Ros</hi>: I have seen a copy of the proposed
                    memorandum from Secretary McNamara to
                    the President which recommends that henceforth defoliation operations in
                    Viet-Nam be conducted under the supervision of the Ambassador and General
                        Harkins.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d313-f2"/> I am agreeable to your indicating Department of State
                    concurrence to the memorandum.</p>
                <p>However, I suggest that we ask for regular reporting from Saigon on the
                    effectiveness of the operation as weighed against the harm being done to United
                    States interests by Communist propaganda on the subject.</p>
                <p>If the President approves the memorandum, I suggest Saigon be informed by a joint
                    State-Defense message.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >Alex</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d313-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d313-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Washington National Records Center, RG 330, OSD Files: FRC 66 A 3542,
                    Vietnam 1962, 370.64. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d313-f2" n="2" xml:id="d313-f2-content">
                <p>The proposed memorandum has not been found; for text as sent to the President on
                    November 16, see <ref target="#d317">Document 317</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
